### B. Virtual Sensor Node Array (Hardware Components Simulated)

Each simulated shipment is monitored by an array of 6 distinct IoT sensor hardware devices:

1. **Primary Reefer IoT Gateway (`sns-sim-xxx-1`)**: High-precision internal temperature & humidity probe mounted inside the primary container.
2. **Secondary BLE Thermal Logger (`sns-sim-xxx-2`)**: Pallet-level Bluetooth Low Energy temperature logging tag.
3. **Container Door Contact Sensor (`sns-sim-xxx-3`)**: Hall-effect magnetic door sensor logging open/close events.
4. **Shock & Vibration Transducer (`sns-sim-xxx-4`)**: 3-axis accelerometer recording mechanical shocks (g) and tilt angles (°).
5. **Satellite / Cellular Telematics Unit (`sns-sim-xxx-5`)**: Long-range GPS and RSSI signal tracker monitoring connectivity status.
6. **Battery & Diagnostics Controller (`sns-sim-xxx-6`)**: Power management node tracking battery voltage decay and internal device clock skew.

### C. Data Reading Schema

Every generated telemetry ping contains 12 parameters:
```typescript
interface SensorReading {
  shipmentId: string;
  sensorId: string;
  timestamp: string;
  temperature: number;      // °C
  humidity: number;         // %
  shock: number;            // g-force
  tilt: number;             // degrees
  latitude: number;         // GPS coord
  longitude: number;        // GPS coord
  signalStrength: number;   // dBm
  batteryLevel: number;     // %
  connectivityStatus: 'Observed' | 'Dropped' | 'Buffered' | 'Unknown';
}
```

